Here is the input problem:
  Axiom 1 (double_1): double(zero) = zero.
  Axiom 2 (half_1): half(zero) = zero.
  Axiom 3 (half_2): half(suc(zero)) = zero.
  Axiom 4 (half_3): half(suc(suc(X))) = suc(half(X)).
  Axiom 5 (double_2): double(suc(X)) = suc(suc(double(X))).
  Axiom 6 (eqNat_1): eqNat(zero, zero) = true.
  Axiom 7 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
  Axiom 8 (eqNat_3): eqNat(suc(X), zero) = false.
  Axiom 9 (eqNat_4): eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) = eqNat(X, Y).
  Axiom 10 (prop_doubleHalf_1): prop_doubleHalf(X) = eqNat(double(half(X)), X).
  Axiom 11 (reflexivity): equals(X, X) = true.
  Axiom 12 (prop_doubleHalf): equals(prop_doubleHalf(X), false) = false.
  Goal 1 (true_equals_false): true = false.

1. double(zero) -> zero
2. half(zero) -> zero
3. half(suc(zero)) -> zero
4. suc(half(X)) -> half(suc(suc(X)))
5. suc(suc(double(X))) -> double(suc(X))
6. eqNat(zero, zero) -> true
7. eqNat(zero, suc(X)) -> false
8. eqNat(suc(X), zero) -> false
9. eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) -> eqNat(X, Y)
10. eqNat(double(half(X)), X) -> prop_doubleHalf(X)
11. equals(X, X) -> true
12. equals(prop_doubleHalf(X), false) -> false
13. prop_doubleHalf(zero) -> true
14. prop_doubleHalf(suc(zero)) -> false
15. false -> true

The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 1 (double_1): double(zero) = zero.
Axiom 2 (half_2): half(suc(zero)) = zero.
Axiom 3 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
Axiom 4 (prop_doubleHalf_1): prop_doubleHalf(X) = eqNat(double(half(X)), X).

Goal 1 (prop_doubleHalf): prop_doubleHalf(X) = false.
The goal is true when:
  X = suc(zero)

Proof:
  prop_doubleHalf(suc(zero))
= { by axiom 4 (prop_doubleHalf_1) }
  eqNat(double(half(suc(zero))), suc(zero))
= { by axiom 2 (half_2) }
  eqNat(double(zero), suc(zero))
= { by axiom 1 (double_1) }
  eqNat(zero, suc(zero))
= { by axiom 3 (eqNat_2) }
  false

RESULT: Theorem (the conjecture is true).
